# Walking a node's detail by card rather than by row.
#
# The screen this is on is the longest list in the client, and until Left and Right meant
# something here the only way down it was Up and Down - a row at a time, past four dozen facts
# no press does anything to. Echo Repeater is seven cards; crossing it by row is twenty-two
# presses and crossing it by card is six.
#
# Two things to watch besides the jump itself. The action bar's A comes and goes: it is named on
# the verbs at the top of the screen and on a reading with a chart behind it, and on nothing
# else, because those are the only rows the press does anything on. And the window now stops a
# look-ahead short of the cursor rather than on it, so a card jumped onto has its heading and
# its first rows on the panel instead of one row at the bottom edge.
#
# Row 0 of the Nodes list is the Map, so a node's row is its index in the demo roster plus one -
# Echo Repeater is seeds[5] and row 6.

scene demo
tab nodes
# The Nodes list has three rows before its first node - the filter chips, the sort row and
# the Map (MESH_UI_NODES_LEAD_ROWS) - so a node's row is its index in the demo roster plus
# three. Echo Repeater is seeds[5] and row 8.
key down 8
key a
hold 1200

# Right, a card per press: Identity, Signal, Environment, Power, then the two neighbour groups.
key right
hold 900
key right
hold 900
key right
hold 900
key right
hold 900
key right
hold 1200

# And back. Left from inside a group is "the top of this one" first, which is why this steps
# down into a card before walking out of it.
key down 1
hold 900
key left
hold 900
key left
hold 900
key left
hold 1600
